WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:05.316
This chapter asks a specific question: Behavioral tests can reveal what

2
00:00:05.316 --> 00:00:10.095
a model did without identifying the internal features, circuits, representations,

3
00:00:10.095 --> 00:00:15.351
or causal pathways that produced it, while interpretability methods can themselves

4
00:00:15.351 --> 00:00:17.740
generate persuasive but unstable stories.

5
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:23.503
The tempting shortcut is insufficient: A probe, visualization, sparse feature label,

6
00:00:23.503 --> 00:00:28.926
attribution map, or circuit diagram is not white-box proof unless it

7
00:00:28.926 --> 00:00:32.870
is reproducible, causally tested, stable under relevant transformations,

8
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.335
scoped to a model/version/data regime,

9
00:00:35.675 --> 00:00:38.830
and compared with plausible alternative explanations.

10
00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:45.100
The chapter's core claim is this: Internal-state observations should enter governance

11
00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.771
only as typed evidence artifacts with lineage, method assumptions, replication status,

12
00:00:50.771 --> 00:00:55.410
causal interventions, stability checks, coverage limits, and explicit non-authority;

13
00:00:55.750 --> 00:01:01.568
white-box evidence complements but does not replace behavioral and operational evidence.

14
00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:07.386
Define an evidence packet containing model hash, dataset slice, method version,

15
00:01:07.386 --> 00:01:10.030
feature/circuit identifiers, assumptions, and confidence.

16
00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:15.874
Separate observational association, predictive decoding, causal necessity, causal sufficiency,

17
00:01:15.874 --> 00:01:21.990
and completeness claims. Require held-out replication across prompts, seeds, checkpoints,

18
00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.825
and relevant transformations.

19
00:01:24.425 --> 00:01:28.455
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

20
00:01:28.795 --> 00:01:33.265
The implemented minimum is a strict internal-evidence packet schema,

21
00:01:33.265 --> 00:01:38.728
one explicitly expired record-shape fixture, a separately implemented semantic consumer with

22
00:01:38.728 --> 00:01:44.192
twelve rejecting mutations, and a finite Lean route that rejects scientifically

23
00:01:44.192 --> 00:01:46.675
incomplete packets, expires changed packets,

24
00:01:47.015 --> 00:01:48.895
and cannot grant authority.

25
00:01:49.235 --> 00:01:54.472
The claim-bearing campaign is prospectively frozen and resource-isolated but unexecuted;

26
00:01:54.472 --> 00:01:59.709
it requires one digest-bound open model, two independently owned methods,

27
00:01:59.709 --> 00:02:04.945
a tuned behavioral baseline, positive and negative controls, causal interventions,

28
00:02:04.945 --> 00:02:07.040
stability and residual accounting,

29
00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:13.570
an independent evaluator, and a one-time held-out opening after seven competence

30
00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:19.197
gates. Separate observational association, predictive decoding, causal necessity, causal sufficiency,

31
00:02:19.197 --> 00:02:20.885
and completeness claims.

32
00:02:21.485 --> 00:02:26.978
The design can still fail. feature hallucination confirmation-biased labeling probe leakage

33
00:02:26.978 --> 00:02:32.472
polysemantic feature collapse The correct response is to stop, narrow, quarantine,

34
00:02:32.472 --> 00:02:37.965
compensate, or retain an owned residual rather than narrate uncertainty away.

35
00:02:38.565 --> 00:02:43.611
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

36
00:02:43.611 --> 00:02:47.740
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

37
00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:52.786
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

38
00:02:52.786 --> 00:02:53.245
closed.

39
00:02:53.585 --> 00:02:58.669
In the finite policy model, no interpretability evidence packet can widen

40
00:02:58.669 --> 00:03:03.291
execution or release authority; it may only preserve, restrict, escalate,

41
00:03:03.291 --> 00:03:04.215
or reject.

42
00:03:04.555 --> 00:03:09.857
Packets with stale lineage, missing method assumptions, absent negative controls,

43
00:03:09.857 --> 00:03:14.629
or unsupported causal state are rejected before governance use.

44
00:03:14.629 --> 00:03:17.810
Labels retain examples, counterexamples, and uncertainty.

45
00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:23.374
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

46
00:03:23.374 --> 00:03:28.338
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

47
00:03:28.338 --> 00:03:33.302
deployment. A local check or formal model does not establish real-world

48
00:03:33.302 --> 00:03:37.815
enforcement. No safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI, or ASI conclusion follows.

49
00:03:38.155 --> 00:03:42.630
These boundaries matter because an explanatory derivative is useful only if

50
00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:45.885
it preserves the evidence ceiling of its source.

51
00:03:46.485 --> 00:03:51.787
At most, this visual explains the chapter's design rationale at argument

52
00:03:51.787 --> 00:03:56.606
support; it adds no empirical, deployment, safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI,

53
00:03:56.606 --> 00:04:01.908
or ASI result. The next chapter is Capability Thresholds and Deployment

54
00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:02.390
Commitments.

55
00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:08.008
It takes responsibility for A system can collect a capability score,

56
00:04:08.008 --> 00:04:13.286
a time-horizon estimate, or a risk-evaluation result without recording which future

57
00:04:13.286 --> 00:04:15.685
safeguard, release constraint, exception authority.
